  year={2022},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={99-103},
  abstract={Artificial intelligence technology assists SPOC to improve effective teaching. It is found through analysis that the SPOC teaching in the design discipline has problems such as weak interactivity, a weak sense of classroom atmosphere, and low control efficiency. The human-machine collaborative and effective teaching model is built with strategies such as human-machine integration and optimization of teaching resources, multi-platform collaborative and interactive experience teaching, online virtual simulation laboratory, an AI partner to help students, and human-machine multi-dimensional evaluation. Thus, it is aimed to explore internal and external factors that influence teaching efficiency, construct an effective teaching model with human-machine coordination, innovate human-machine integration and optimization of teaching resources, and strengthen the strategies in multi-platform collaborative and interactive experience teaching. Online virtual simulation laboratory, AI partner-aided teaching, human-machine multi-dimensional evaluation, and other aspects jointly are used to construct the SPOC Teaching. Then, teaching moves toward the SPOC Teaching for precise teaching, effective control, and in-depth learning The students’ autonomous learning ability is stimulated to adapt to the diversified future. Artificial intelligence technology provides a new idea to SPOC effective teaching for intelligent development.},
  keywords={Adaptation models;Analytical models;Distance learning;Atmospheric modeling;Education;Social sciences;Collaboration;Artificial Intelligence;SPOC;effective teaching;interactive experience;AI Aided Teaching},
  doi={10.1109/SSIM55504.2022.10047942},
