  title={A Collaborative Optimization Framework for AAV-Enabled Visible Light Communication Systems in Post-Disaster Relief}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-16},
  abstract={Natural disasters such as earthquakes, floods, and fires often lead to the disruption of wireless communications infrastructure and the deterioration of the electromagnetic environment, which can ultimately lead to disaster relief failure. Therefore, this paper proposes an air–ground cooperative communication-lighting system that integrates autonomous aerial vehicle (AAV) with visible light communication (VLC) technologies. With its flexible deployment and strong environmental adaptability, the system enables rapid deployment of emergency communication networks, simultaneously providing lighting services after disasters. However, the system faces multiple challenges in task scheduling, communication performance assurance, energy management, and service continuity in post-disaster deployment. To address these challenges, we design a cooperative optimization framework based on the twin delayed deep deterministic policy gradient (TD3) and dynamic adaptive particle swarm optimization (DAPSO), and introduce an energy-aware mechanism for joint optimization of AAV trajectory control and hover deployment. The framework enables efficient switching and coordination mechanisms between environmental uncertainties and diversified service objects. It not only provides continuous and stable communication and lighting services but also takes into account energy efficiency. Simulation results verify that the proposed framework significantly improves system performance, achieving 11.2% lower energy consumption compared with traditional RF schemes while improving the average data rate by 2.9% and illumination quality by 7.4%.},
  keywords={Autonomous aerial vehicles;Optimization;Lighting;Trajectory;Disasters;Visible light communication;Energy efficiency;Energy consumption;Collaboration;Vehicle dynamics;Autonomous aerial vehicle (AAV);trajectory planning;position optimization;intelligent decision and control;visible light communication(VLC)},
